A **line graph** (both variables are continuous):
- $x$-axis (independent variable): "Number of wraps in myelin sheath", even scale 0–5;
- $y$-axis (dependent variable): "Conduction velocity (m s$^{-1}$)", even scale 0–2.0;
- all five points plotted accurately as crosses;
- a smooth **curve of best fit** through the points that does not extend beyond the data (not started at the origin) and has no arrowheads;
- a title, e.g. "Effect of myelin sheath thickness on conduction velocity".
